l,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e6fa516e4d88ddfcf3650b3a09fd6124574d2dc42889573c0bf8eca6c9f50822","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"Procedure","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"80fe4a348ffda1a68aa603c83704833166f5576300fbdc4c44207daeca24a8d9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Date of updates","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.1","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"83ec34a74df59c435257cd2dbbf56bee56831d9470fa5a89bfe755dd51f5338e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.1","title":"Season start","body":"● Each Season will start with the most up-to-date rules all documents will hold a change log and version number the version is equal to the year and the month the version was created\n● Over the course of that season, the Documents/ FAQ will be updated.\n● This may be due to spelling mistakes, rules not being written the best they can be, or new rules that have not been foreseen.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.1.1","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"390ddaf6b5a85f45fa8af51f23a4018664f7b9bc7afa658a747f112a460e0375","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1.2","title":"Season end","body":"At the end of the current season, the Errata/FAQ will be merged into the current rules for the upcoming season.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.1.2","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a3d019cadd5c4f79b954addb137553efa0d336c325f65263e34073cab8a311db","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Rule changes","body":"The Buhurt International committees and board with the NO's will oversee the Errata/FAQ process as follows:","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.2","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e89617d7e1c2d1ee74708dcf544c455e5c226f1d3f5079265f562094929c5425","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.1","title":"Minor Change","body":"A minor change involves rewording parts of the rules to make them clearer without changing how they are applied. The Committees will discuss and rewrite any rules.\nThese will be updated in the document on the website, including the date of publication and the document version. The updated documents will be sent to every registered member on our website. These changes are intended to clarify the rules, not to make major alterations.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.2.1","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"977c37efaad2f2fccce9d02e0099c6a1d9b964e4f399e36c2a3639532678ba33","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.2","title":"Major Change","body":"For major changes, the Committees will draft the rules and present them to the Buhurt International Board, which will then discuss them with the National Organizations (NO).\nThese changes will be voted on by the NO.\n\nExamples of major changes include any modification with a direct impact on:\n● Allowed or prohibited techniques.\n● Points counting.\n● Technical requirements for armor and weapons (length, weight, etc.).\n● Any changes that have a financial impact on our members.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.2.2","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"001222bf9b3b02166b12277d383d8f739594b8d5298e81f96dad6e2495933f5b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"Feedback","body":"Rules feedback can be done by all Buhurt International Members on our Website. This is the best way to let us know of any concerns. These will then be given to the Marshal Committee to look at.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:1.3","parent_key":"rule-update-policy:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"59486abdef5ee220cf8588ee1af331252195f07493b7f284614330d7ca58f9d9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"2","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nMarch 2024 (Version update from 2024.03 to 2024.06)\n\nUpdate date: June-2024\n- clearification: 1.2.1 Minor change\n- clearification: 1.2.2 Major change Update date: March-2024\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"rule-update-policy:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2fe981e323a2daf47009fb9497abad0a375d3648946a809325cde06094e57b71","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","release":"2026-10-06","inventory_key":"executive/structure-accreditation-titles","synthetic":false,"version":{"version":"December 2024","title":"Committees Structure, Accreditation and Titles V2024.12","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"The document prints no version number. Its changelog's latest entry is \"Update date: December-2024\"; the label is that date. (The file name used for the source drop says \"V2024.12\".)","source_url":"https://www.buhurtinternational.com/_files/ugd/d219c5_ffce59b9558045d8a5dec698616e1b21.pdf","source_sha256":"401cf406309543d3fb0454b9b2d43b3da92544374e33e0793a8ac035c4990a2b","retrieved_at":"2026-10-06T00:00:00Z","page_count":8,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"9476b39e2a8ad37cc26301519977324635acc87bacc7d0acdf17b570bef79544","detected":{"version":null,"date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 import), read from the official PDF: cover, page footers and changelog","reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["page(s) without extractable text: 1"],"pages":8,"source_lines":157,"assigned_lines":219,"furniture_lines":27,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99718,"provisions":21,"numbered":19,"needs_review":0,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[1],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"figure","number":null,"title":null,"body":"","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:page-1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":"cover page: artwork only, no text","topics":["cover"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"Committees Structure, Accreditations and Titles A committee is a group of people appointed for a specific function. Buhurt International uses Committees to handle the tasks needed to be performed. Committees can be Marshal Committee, Authenticity Committee, Judiciary Committee, etc.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4ae32f352bb4748134bd888bca5e412b107d75a30d2b39f7d24627bfc6dfda8c","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General structure","body":"Committees include members with sufficient accreditation and are overseen by a Council.\nMembers' accreditation are defined at article 2","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["2"],"content_sha256":"44d3a942c9978465c29395fec9248a6dfbc9049134ac40ee71d3211f513db169","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Structure of Committees","body":"Committees of Buhurt International are structured vertically in 3 levels:\n●International: overseen by the Council ●Conference: overseen by Conference Head and Deputy Conference Head Head ●Regional: overseen by Regional Head","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.1","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["3"],"content_sha256":"68ddfe63a6732eb8f735c23d983927a30ad51fd3d09589468d368acb6b6ff1f2","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Internal structure","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"acc80084ce5197a1ec602d79997a36b306ed3db51e0599d0b3dbb55461205343","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.1","title":"International","body":"●The Committees are led by a Council. The Council serves as the head of the Committees.\nIts members have decision-making authority and lead the Committees in its endeavors.\n\n●The Council is led by an International Head and a Deputy International Head.\n\n●The Council is responsible for organizing General Meetings for decision-making purposes and Council Meetings as needed.\n\n●The Council is tasked with sanctioning rules infractions.\n\n●The Council includes every Committee's members with the accreditation of Conference Head and Deputy Conference Head.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2.1","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c5dbc9f27755cb2efde836fc1f2b247c42e86d803433368560cee38198e68c8f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.2","title":"Conference","body":"●Conference level is led by a Conference Head and Deputy Conference Head members.\nThose people are in charge of their Conference (i.e APAC, North American, Europe etc.).\n\n●The Conference Head and Deputy Conference Head are tasked with organizing their committee’s work on the conference level.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2.2","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f4b9e5df4480f2764e0bc404d9379c268d2e51041fe474a1a89c001a611bb2ce","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.3","title":"Regional","body":"●National level is led by a Regional Head. Those people are in charge of their Region (i.e UK, Germany, Australia etc.).\n\n●The Regional Head is tasked with their committee’s work on the regional level.\n\n●Regional level is also the gathering of all Committee’s members no matter their accreditation for its specific Region.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2.3","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4ecab06a8d3bd5bc7085ad07795867ce6c613c85f689e12e55110ea2ae65df6e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.4","title":"Advisors","body":"●The Committees can include Advisors. These individuals act as counselors, sharing their knowledge and expertise as experts in their respective fields.\n\n●While they are not formal members of the Committees and do not hold an accreditation, they are permitted to participate in discussions and contribute to the Committee's work.\n\n●Advisors are eligible to attend General Meetings but are not entitled to vote.\n\n●Advisors are designated by the Council of the committee.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2.4","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f9f0783b3388a70d4535f060339fc6f8754f89e6232957476af5f835dc406fda","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Member Accreditation And Titles","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c0cd69757420b371b9e872dc5519b596698f7ddb375a39cddef142ca522aaa1d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"Members of the Committees","body":"Members of the Committees can have different accreditation depending on their experience.\nEach Committee is responsible for graduating its members according to their accreditation system. Each accreditation rewards the experience, knowledge and skills of members.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b0f7abcf765a3919cd1ec764529bf4ac6598ae0c0a4494be36203e2100ef4df4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.1","title":"Trainees","body":"●Trainees are individuals new to the Committee's missions, who are enthusiastic about participating and learning.\n\n●They are in a developmental phase and contribute to the work of the Committees.\n\n●They are eligible to participate in the General Meetings but do not possess voting rights.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1.1","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6ab27bd699d37e93cbaac561e79fb960ad9709c0831c8f17c598919b2fa33c29","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.2","title":"Regional","body":"●Once trainees have sufficient experience, they can be rewarded by Regional accreditation.\n\n●They are now active members of the Committees and participate in the Committee’s mission.\n\n●They are eligible to participate in the General Meetings and possess voting rights.\n\n●Regional Head is responsible for promotion from Trainee to Regional accreditation, according to the committee’s accreditation regulation.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1.2","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f13b5d38d3ae84a72dfad32ff9df63984df954aefa7af16b6ca27fdf8d13d566","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.3","title":"Conference","body":"●They are experienced members that participate actively in the Committee’s projects.\n\n●They should be able to communicate in English with every person involved in Buhurt International.\n\n●They are eligible to participate in the General Meetings and possess voting rights.\n\n●Conference Head and Deputy Conference Head Head are responsible for promotion from Regional to Conference accreditation, according to the committee’s accreditation regulation.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1.3","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"022230f7cb11c6a0762d70fa0504c7801e531991250ed0553eaab1465e7f9124","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.4","title":"International","body":"●They are the most experienced members of the Committees, they constitute its primary workforce.\n\n●They engage in Committee activities under the supervision of the Council.\n\n●They should be able to communicate in English with every person involved in Buhurt International. They are eligible to participate in the General Meetings and possess voting rights.\n\n●Council members are responsible for promotion from Conference to International accreditation, according to the committee’s accreditation regulation.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1.4","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"744681fe2807b2dee80fc8a32940e5e29e1cb763bb350e5792bf7d324656b2aa","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Titles","body":"Committee Members can have a title, showing their role among the organization of the committee.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3747d14c6dfa4544b49eea89b3a46a1a3b9551b0b4bc94e2e5f0c9740506fe72","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.1","title":"International Head and Deputy International Head","body":"●The International Head holds the responsibility of leading its Committee. This includes presenting the committee’s decisions to the Buhurt International Board, the General Assembly, and the community.\n\n●The International Head presides over meetings, coordinates the agenda, facilitates discussions, and ensures the equal participation of all members.\n\n●Collaborating closely with other Committee’s Members, the International Head ensures that committee decisions and actions align with established goals and guidelines.\n\n●The International Head is elected by the General Assembly of Buhurt International and serves three-year terms.\n\n●The International Head and Deputy International Head must have the accreditation of International within their Committee and have the Conference Head title.\n\n●During meetings, the International Head possesses a vote with a weight of two for decision-making.\n\n●In the event that the International Head is unable to fulfill their duties for a period exceeding three months, the Deputy International Head assumes leadership of the Council.\n\n●The Deputy International Head is nominated by the Council and serves a two-year term, similar to other Council members.\n\n●The Deputy International Head shares the same duties with the International Head.","page_from":6,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2.1","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f1185e92378ae60c1a930f2e5b83fcfb770dc9880562ca45aa7330428576be16","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.2","title":"Council members","body":"●Council Members are responsible for leading the Committees, organizing meetings, and overseeing the various projects essential to the committee’s work.\n\n●Council Members work closely with other Committee’s Members to ensure that committee decisions and actions are in line with established goals and guidelines.\n\n●Council Members are elected by Committee Members assembled in General Meetings.\n\n●Council Members serve two-year terms, and only members with International accreditations can be elected as Council members.\n\n●Each Council Member possesses one vote with a weight of two for decision-making.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2.2","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9b7a3e3213865d2e73170efdc6dccd9056104d66c5c4c79a9d4f24c44b14ec79","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.3","title":"Conference Head and Deputy Head","body":"●They are, esteemed for their extensive experience within the Committees, play a vital role in guiding the Council by overseeing other Committee’s Members, facilitating their growth, and actively participating in projects led by the Council.\n\n●Promotion to Conference Head / Deputy Head is determined through a vote by the Council, considering factors such as experience, knowledge, and contributions to the Committees.\n\n●Each Conference Head / Deputy Head possesses one vote with a weight of two in decision-making during General Meetings.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2.3","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"408898245c068e6fdd3a8882ea061c780b8d06fd4334c71c3918d9c61c70e0e3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.4","title":"Regional Head","body":"●Regional Head are experienced members of the Committees who actively participate in discussions and hold voting privileges.\n\n●Regional Head selection is determined through a vote by their Conference Head, considering factors such as experience, knowledge, and contributions to the Committee.\n\n●Regional Head possesses one vote with a weight of two in decision-making during meetings.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2.4","parent_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b0e01744bb82a8fbd0fd8b9fb392468b93e2c0ca59ee9d1ac8585a9fc9c8d551","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"3","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules\n\nUpdate date: December-2024\n- add: changelog and formatting\n- change: Ranks to Accreditation Update date: January-2024\n- add: Document created","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"structure-accreditation-titles:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"29b887a77c96aa8f5d486e468a325817ff4a775c9a511145d4dd1459ccf97349","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","release":"2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/accreditation","synthetic":false,"version":{"version":"2025.03","title":"Marshal Accreditation","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Changelog: latest entry \"March-2025 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2025.03)\".","source_url":"https://www.buhurtinternational.com/_files/ugd/53cbbd_aadb219ddd34443c817c2c5f6236a6a9.pdf","source_sha256":"163ae6660527c5e3d9a7de5bfbc7ceb9a3a9ea3608b918426577037790e464b6","retrieved_at":"2026-10-06T00:00:00Z","page_count":9,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"d2b2d1a5f7aefed2fe24f59b8ea8f121659c848f724f9b9d856658d5059e11b8","detected":{"version":null,"date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 import), read from the official PDF: cover, page footers and changelog","reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["page(s) without extractable text: 1"],"pages":9,"source_lines":220,"assigned_lines":267,"furniture_lines":19,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99801,"provisions":21,"numbered":19,"needs_review":0,"verified":1,"empty_pages":[1],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"figure","number":null,"title":null,"body":"","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"accreditation:page-1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":"cover page: artwork only, no text","topics":["cover"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":null,"title":null,"body":"Marshal accreditation","page_from":2,"page_to":2,"stable_key":"accreditation:p0001","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["introduction"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5eaf7e6e11144c9d54ff6a0eec824426db12699ec750058473eec2cbfa203f07","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"Accreditation Levels","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6e9d607e0b1e9b02f95174c9b218d7926b96e7ae661b72d0d8c35eaabfb4b690","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Trainee - Level 4","body":"A Trainee Marshal is the first step toward achieving international accreditation as a marshal. For further details, please refer to the Marshal Accreditation document.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:1.1","parent_key":"accreditation:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0f2cf5e71a3fa9b8db09382525c24176040b578ed0b179078844191f6359e544","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Regional - Level 3","body":"A Regional Marshal is an individual who has gained experience working at multiple events, successfully passed the Trainee test, and is now qualified to marshal inside the list.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:1.2","parent_key":"accreditation:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"aa2333d468bc216b8d9ddd06b595fb33abac857668cfbd273dfdb7fed379096b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"Conference - Level 2","body":"A Conference Marshal is an individual with extensive knowledge of the rules and has worked at various events. They have completed their exam, Interview and are on track for International accreditation.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:1.3","parent_key":"accreditation:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"399ab8ba699bc78e61cdb81d32c270a5bb46328d22b5bd8ac8df5983b965546b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.4","title":"International - Level 1","body":"An International Marshal is the final level of accreditation, achieved by individuals with extensive experience in high-level events and demonstrating exceptional skills and knowledge.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:1.4","parent_key":"accreditation:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ffd646ba820eedd095c5a3dd90058ecb926484cc8e11f78884c90d73e85b94f7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Marshal Accreditation","body":"Marshal accreditation is the process by which our Sport accredits its marshals from Trainee to International Marshal.\nThis eight (8) stages process will ensure that our regions have a high standard of marshals for Buhurt International events.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"79f988e74fdf8895f8276d6da5208a48b651333dcbe3b52ee8b73d8082d43570","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"Stages overview","body":"Stage 1 – Learning the rules Stage 2 – Working at events with an accredited International Marshal Stage 3 – Taking the Regional Marshal accreditation test Stage 4 – Working at one event with a Conference Head Marshal or assigned Representative Stage 5 – Taking the Conference Marshal accreditation test Stage 6 – Interviewing with a Conference Head Marshal Stage 7 – Becoming an accredited Conference Marshal Stage 8 – Becoming an accredited International Marshal","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:2.1","parent_key":"accreditation:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f09d3ea77c84bfb3a8a2d8476012a34eff15bbb6355afbbe5cc22ffd8107a4e0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Stage 1: Learning the rules","body":"Marshal trainees are not permitted in the list while fighting is occurring.\nBefore they can work in the list, marshal trainees will need to read all the rules from Buhurt International. Below are some ideas to help you:\n● Download and print all rules and regulations found on the Buhurt International website.\n● Ask your Regional Head Marshal questions on rules you are unsure of.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"accreditation:2.2","parent_key":"accreditation:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f15c19e12a5e456c273bb18948fa2fcd4283b0b1166eb453bbef7037140c2aa0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Stage 2: Working at events with an accredited International Marshal","body":"To qualify as a Regional Marshal, a trainee marshal must participate in one of the following options:\nThree (3) tournaments, ensuring they have experience in the following categories at least once:\n● Buhurt\n● Duels\n● Outrance (optional) Two (2) tournaments, and one (1) official Buhurt International training event (in person seminar) with a Regional/Deputy Conference/Conference Head Marshal. Ensuring they have experience in the following categories at least once:\n● Buhurt\n● Duels\n● Outrance (optional) Marshal trainees will be paired with a Regional Marshal, a Conference Marshal or an International Marshal to learn from them.\nBelow are some ideas to help you:\n● Observe the accredited Marshals’ work in and out of the list.\n● Talk and ask questions to the Marshal you are paired with, and to the knight marshal.\n● Participate in all marshaling activities of the event (e.g. weapons check, armor check, counting duels and buhurt observation).","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"accreditation:2.3","parent_key":"accreditation:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"24460b191eb3b574810e5b56f15e98428a80d059e83c3fdfefdc02a7baef01e0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"Stage 3: Taking the Regional Marshal accreditation test","body":"Once the marshal trainee has worked at the required number of events, they will be able to take the regional accreditation test, which consists of ten (10) questions.\nThe test will cover:\n● buhurt,\n● duels,\n● weapon’s basic authenticity rules.\nIf they have passed the test:\n● They are now accredited Regional Marshal.\n● They will be given a Regional Marshal certificate.\n● They are allowed to work as either a line marshal or a field marshal.\nBelow are some ideas to help you.\n1. Talk and ask questions to the knight marshal.\n2. Study all Buhurt International rules and regulations sets.\n3.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"accreditation:2.4","parent_key":"accreditation:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ef8b0c663eef8e7fe26ce7c2747515564c331ba03380a131c3e7530ccd32d044","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Stage 4: Working at one event with a Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head","body":"Marshal To become a Conference Marshal, a Regional Marshal will be required to work:\n● at one (1) event with the Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal,\n● on all aspects of marshaling at this event (e.g. weapons check, armor check, counting duels and buhurt observation).\nAfter the event, the Conference Head Marshal or Deputy Conference Head will let the Regional Marshal know if they are ready to take the conference accreditation test or if they need to participate in another event with them.\nBelow are some ideas to help you:\n● Talk and ask questions to the knight marshal.\n● Participate in all marshaling activities of the event.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"accreditation:3.1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"verified","review_note":"The official document numbers stages 4 to 8 as 3.1 to 3.5 without printing a section 3 heading (its table of contents lists them as 2.1 to 2.5; the next printed section is \"4. Marshal accreditation checklist\"). Kept as printed. The heading wraps: its last word \"Marshal\" begins the text.","topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f47fd0a63feef3a85c7bcb090f316195a01f84b5b38767a0bf62133d8f0f1703","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Stage 5: Taking the conference marshal accreditation test","body":"Once the Regional Marshal has worked at the required number of events, they will be able to take the conference accreditation test, which consists of forty (40) questions.\nThe test will cover:\n● buhurt,\n● duels,\n● weapon’s basic authenticity rules.\nBelow are some ideas to help you.\n● Talk and ask questions to the knight marshal.\n● Study all Buhurt International rules and regulations sets.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"accreditation:3.2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"529f4b3d7d66681f939342f478a8f6d06cd0c3e26fdeafec8cfcf22aa4aafd53","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"Stage 6: Interviewing with a Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal","body":"Once the Regional Marshal has completed the conference accreditation test, they will have an interview with their Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal.\nIn this interview, the wrong and/or incomplete answers from the test will be reviewed, and the Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal may ask further questions.\nBelow are some ideas to help you.\n● Be thorough and honest in your answers.\n● The Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal is there to help you, not to fail you.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"accreditation:3.3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"01c7228cb72b5074529f126af566357a036987b63049963c24e0791f7f4e6432","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"Stage 7: Becoming an accredited Conference Marshal","body":"If the Regional Marshal has failed the conference accreditation test and/or interview:\n● They keep their regional accreditation.\n● They will need to repeat stages 4, 5 and 6 again until they receive their conference accreditation.\nIf they have passed the test and the interview:\n● They are now accredited Conference Marshal.\n● They will be given a Conference Marshal certificate.\n● They are allowed to work as either a line marshal, a field marshal, or a knight marshal.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"accreditation:3.4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"84afd5e3db9a765b9ecb0732d6c87bf32b46e58180f7d64e3b8faef6a2d65d01","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Stage 8: Becoming an accredited International Marshal","body":"The International Marshal accreditation is the highest accreditation a marshal can obtain.\nBefore a marshal can attempt the International Marshal accreditation process, they must have:\n● A Conference Marshal accreditation.\n● 2 video recordings of them working at 2 separate Buhurt International events.\nOnce the Buhurt International Marshal Committee has reviewed the 2 recordings, the Committee will have an interview with the marshal, in which they will go over any questions they have about the videos. The committee may also ask any other questions that they may have.\n● Video recordings\n● These events may be from the Regional and Conference Marshal Process.\n● These videos must be given to the Buhurt International Marshal Committee to review.\n● The Buhurt International Marshal Committee will review these videos to make sure the Marshal is at a particular skill level.\n\nIf you have failed your Interview process\n● You will continue being a Conference Marshal.\n● You will need to repeat the Buhurt International Marshal Accreditation Process until you receive your accreditation.\n\nIf you have passed your Interview,\n● You are now an Internationally Accredited Marshal.\n● This means you are allowed to work in Buhurt International events that require this particular Accreditation.\n● You will be given a Buhurt International Marshal Certificate.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"accreditation:3.5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b7210f5400f2c033f3ac5379dc777f865fce73ce5fb1eedb487e16e0d0cf8198","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Marshal accreditation checklist","body":"STAGE 1 LEARNING THE RULES\n\nACCREDITED INTERNATIONAL MARSHAL SIGNATURE: _____________________\n\nSTAGE 2 WORK AT EVENTS WITH ACCREDITED INTERNATIONAL MARSHAL\n\nEVENT 1: ____________________________ DATE: _________ ACCREDITED INTERNATIONAL MARSHAL SIGNATURE: _____________________\n\nEVENT 2: ____________________________ DATE: _________ ACCREDITED INTERNATIONAL MARSHAL SIGNATURE: _____________________\n\nEVENT 3 : ____________________________ DATE: _________ ACCREDITED INTERNATIONALl MARSHAL SIGNATURE: _____________________\n\nSTAGE 3 TAKE THE REGIONAL MARSHAL ACCREDITATION TEST\n\nEVENT: _____________________________ DATE: _________ SCORE: _____________________________ FAIL/PASS: ______ REGIONAL HEAD, DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD OR CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL SIGNATURE: _____________________\n\nSTAGE 4 WORK AT AN EVENT WITH CONFERENCE HEAD OR DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL\n\nEVENT: _____________________________ DATE: _________\n\nCONFERENCE HEAD or DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL SIGNATURE:\n____________________\n\nSTAGE 5 TAKE THE CONFERENCE MARSHAL ACCREDITATION TEST\n\nEVENT: _____________________________ DATE: _________ SCORE: _____________________________ FAIL/PASS: ______\n\nCONFERENCE HEAD or DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL SIGNATURE:\n___________________\n\nSTAGE 6 INTERVIEW WITH CONFERENCE HEAD OR DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL\n\nEVENT: _____________________________ DATE: _________\n\nCONFERENCE HEAD or DEPUTY CONFERENCE HEAD MARSHAL SIGNATURE:\n___________________\n\nSTAGE 7 – BECOMING ACCREDITED CONFERENCE MARSHAL\n\nSTAGE 8 – INTERNATIONAL MARSHAL ACCREDITATION","page_from":7,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"accreditation:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d596cd3f0bc217f395a4bed495b48f2ec9d7db3003aee2e381717fd7c9265c82","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Absence of Regional Head Marshal","body":"If there is no Regional Head Marshal in a Country or Region, the Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal for that country or region will be responsible for the training of marshals until a Regional Head Marshal is appointed.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"accreditation:4.1","parent_key":"accreditation:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"90ae27b6282db154dc985e5cf978a52b935540a76f5fcf29530d0aaaf557127e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Marshal Accreditation Timeframes","body":"There are no time frames on how long it takes to reach each Level of accreditation. There is no requirement to maintain Marshal Accreditation, except for International Accredited Marshals who are required to Marshal 2 Buhurt International Events per calendar year.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"accreditation:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f53db58ed5fa54415781e00faae0b06fbfecc18ca21412b17a74e0a1d2916816","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"6","title":"Change log","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and we will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way, we keep transparent communication and clarity about the rules.\nMarch-2025 (Version update from 2024.06 to 2025.03)\n- format: general formatting and grammar control\n- Replaced: maintain Marshal Accreditation, except for International Accredited Marshals who are required to Marshal 2 Buhurt International Events per calendar year. || There are no time frames on how long it takes to reach each Level of accreditation. There is no requirement to maintain Marshal Accreditation, except for International Accredited Marshals who are required to Marshal 2 Buhurt International Events per calendar year.\n– add: 1. Accreditation Levels\n\nDecember 2024 (Version update from 2024.03 to 2024.06)\n- add 2.0 Marshal accreditation checklist: through all stages: accredited International, deputy conference head\n- add: 1.1.6 Stage 6: Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal\n- add: 1.1.4 Stage 4: Working at one event with a Conference Head or Deputy Conference Head Marshal\n- add: 1.1.2 Stage 2: Two (2) tournaments : (in person seminar) with a Regional/Deputy Conference/Conference Head Marshal\n- Replaced: 1.1 Stages overview - stage 2: Working at events with an accredited International Marshal Regional Head Marshal\n- add:Stage 4 – Working at one event with a Conference Head Marshal or assigned Representative\n- format: grammer June 2024 (Version update from 2024.03 to 2024.06)\n- format: grammer March 2024 (Version update from 2024.01 to 2024.03)\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"accreditation:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"82695d8c8987900c24014d90607a6a8fd44f4a15f5377390048f4d6c42008c22","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","release":"2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/buhurt-rules","synthetic":false,"version":{"version":"26.4.1","title":"Buhurt Rules 26.4.1","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Every page footer \"V. 26.4.1\"; changelog entry \"April - 2026 (V. 26.4.1)\".","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1peAGsMBV8ldNkSlgR-U33V0JqCFYL8ja/view?usp=drive_link","source_sha256":"b019f927ac23bdc57acf58e4262e6c48f450a3689c3feea4b2988f2022ec245d","retrieved_at":"2026-10-06T00:00:00Z","page_count":14,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"7e058aeacc91c0905f744cfbb67b04dce6fa5ddd0b045bb15df9b5cb08ae3f2b","detected":{"version":"26.4.1","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 import), read from the official PDF: cover, page footers and changelog","reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["page(s) without extractable text: 1"],"pages":14,"source_lines":295,"assigned_lines":409,"furniture_lines":22,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99588,"provisions":59,"numbered":58,"needs_review":0,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[1],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"figure","number":null,"title":null,"body":"","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:page-1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":"cover page: artwork only, no text","topics":["cover"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"General Provisions","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d3460a1bce22168eb4fc581713c7f54838f7f6aa5be599e1b9b2b4e8ddc14938","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Criteria for Participation","body":"Competitors must be of legal age in their country and the tournament hosting country.\nDeclare they are medically fit to fight prior to participation in the fight.\nA competitor must sign the disclaimer document (which states that the fighter is aware of the risks associated with participation and acknowledges that the organizer provides no warranties, that they have read the rules and agree to comply).","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"644defbceb7a0414824703a4fda56c2c2e04fbd75ffba320886815e715720e09","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Scoring System Overview","body":"The grounded position of all the opposing team fighters is the main victory criteria in group battles.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2bd1e2b198f5ab7f9fc08fafccc53d700a61c5bd6a5c1efa94d875d0a820e790","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3","title":"Grounding Competitor","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"65cc3008c048a03f90f2bf129dabdafb18bd37b90257c7802166bd6837cc223f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.1","title":"Cases for Grounding","body":"The competitor is grounded in the following cases:\n● They touched the ground with torso, hip, arm, hand, knee, shield except with their two feet.\n\n● They touched a grounded fighter for support with downward pressure.\n\n● If the list has no bottom rail touching the ground, and they fell or stepped with both feet completely out/under the list. Marshals visually determine the boundary of the list.\n\n● Armour failure: if an element of the equipment cannot perform its protective function or is lost, the fighter shall be grounded by marshals. This includes helmet, neck protection (gorget), torso protection (a brigandine, a breastplate, etc), shoulder, elbow, forearm defense, gauntlet, groin protection, shin, thigh, a sabaton, knee-cop, upper arm defense.\n\n● While not carrying a weapon in their hand, they engaged in offensive actions like striking, pushing, grappling, or tripping, directed at an opponent. Holding a shield is not considered holding a weapon.\n\n● They took a reserve weapon from a squire beyond an allocated weapon distribution zone, or inside of the fenced list area, or, if the list has a wide top bar, collected it in any way other than picking it up from the surface of the bar in the allocated area.\n\n● If the list is a wide top bar, they had their full body and legs on top of the list.\n\n● They were grounded by a marshal as a result of the rules violation.\n\n● They yielded by kneeling, voluntarily withdrawing from a fight.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1.3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3f46fd29088aa284bc338874b02686955e2038b5df46f61165d91a80d157b602","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.3.2","title":"Cases for not Grounding","body":"The competitor is not grounded in the following cases:\n● They touched the ground during or immediately after a successful takedown with one of the following cases:\n○ Edge of their shield (not a flat part), ○ Hand (open hand), ○ Fist (closed hand) .\n● They touched their immediate opponent (a fighter they are grappling/falling together with) with any point of contact except for their torso, hips, or buttocks immediately after a successful throw.\n● If the remaining protective elements can compensate for an armor failure.\nExample:\nIf the armor failure occurs to buttocks protection, cuisses that are supplementing a skirt or back elements of a greave.\n● They touched the ground with any part of a weapon.","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:1.3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:1.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8eb8ebfb7ed621ccd019f3e39a16e83208fdb2ddfbbf4a9d389d78f88ea12341","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Authorized Equipment","body":"These rules aim to ensure a high standard of authenticity, safety, and historical accuracy in the equipment and conduct of the participants.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"52165a13d736040e5ee28849d42d66077a07a61d4e408154ef2f18480399ab8a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"General Requirements","body":"Reference all Authenticity Committee documents for the detailed rules.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f8f01dede10d3d59f98c3449b05bb2d4bbfc69b34560ad222048f6ece5263afb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.1","title":"Technical and Authentic Compliance","body":"All equipment must meet Buhurt International technical and authentic requirements.\nReference:\n● “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” document for the rules.\n● ”Technical Requirements for Weapons” document.\n● ”Technical Requirements for Armors” document.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"94ff86c20a1dc19200f2ffb0f47827a392b577291ad04599dc989d1068dbd125","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.2","title":"Competitor Eligibility","body":"Competitors are not allowed unless they have passed technical and authenticity checks.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f998c2926314188a9d0243879aa3168560e3c06c360f95e905f04c9524db56cb","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.3","title":"Weapon Requirements","body":"Reference ”Technical Requirements for Weapons” document for all the rules.\nReference “Weapons/Shield Chart” document for sizes and weights.\nReminder: Low-quality, dirty, rusty, or historically implausible weapons are not allowed.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fc7983039a413f1ed92927364ef427e427d06fdc98e6350dbca1cbb1973f216a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.4","title":"Footwear","body":"Reference ”Textiles and Leather” document for details.\nReminder: Only medieval Shoes with low profile (non-lugged/studded/spiked) are allowed.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"51a46d12fb1cd82c106555f7f279c638eca00243340366f6b1576cbdebf526c2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.5","title":"Materials","body":"Reference ”Textiles and Leather” document for details.\nReminder: Modern adhesive tape, plastic ties, and other visible modern materials are not permitted.\nTextile adhesive tape of neutral colors for kit repair is an exception.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.5","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a7f9020a1f5f1a242416179895ff0c9d6756ccdf481c8220506be3a97100342d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.6","title":"Decorations","body":"Reference “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” for details.\nReminder: Slogans and imagery on equipment should be historically plausible and not derogatory.\nNo modern equipment or decorations are allowed.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1.6","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8f8b18f061791aeee4e74574c1df41e9f0ec32be7169071f69870f457c8e8f5d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Specifics on Weapons and Shields","body":"All Buhurt International weapons and shields are permitted.\nAny combination of these weapons is allowed.\nReference:\n● “Shields and Bucklers” document.\n● “Technical Requirements for Weapons” and specific documents for each weapon type.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5cd1f808c41ceaa801815d1add3d4ed0074da73a4b501293c0cfad157757352f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Equipment Changes","body":"Participants are allowed to change elements of equipment (armor or weapon) during the time between rounds and/or matches.\nTechnical Marshal supervision is required for equipment changes.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"27a28478776d7a2897c7785c44d8acc91b3346eef49b83b2ef0986cc1b3dbfef","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.4","title":"Marshal Authority","body":"The Head Marshal and Authenticity Representative have the authority to demand changes to any element of armor or weapon for safety, aesthetic, or historical accuracy reasons.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:2.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"dff6f1027908290545e4011b85c85fba5d6115e33e7f63aac380e47e1a23acf6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Authorized Fighting Techniques","body":"","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"59c53615fc905448a54cbed7a3a897b407335f644f07bb98ccbd57b895502517","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Permitted Strikes","body":"Strikes are permitted with any part of the weapon, shield, and various body parts (arms, legs and head).\nA competitor can strike with a free hand provided they have a weapon in the other hand. That is at the ready and unsheathed.\nA competitor can strike an opponent who has lost their weapon.\nA competitor can strike an out of balance opponent before they are grounded.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8410f2ad46cbfa743630be0e01355dfa73ed1f211d99fd03a3c82f9ae285f5ca","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Strike Zones","body":"Strikes are allowed to any area not mentioned as a prohibited strike zone (see Section 5 below).","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5"],"content_sha256":"eb0ec8dc2dccb0c9121a54b1e4a16f8a1639dc5b7d7905f5db37a3a4cf87b428","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"Weapon-Grabbing","body":"Grabbing the opponent's weapon (except the blade) or shield with a free hand is permitted. You may not grab the blade of any weapon.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e43064bed77183cc26c4219820f03e3aa6e1266011754533d25d7d4b99586d3e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"Techniques and Moves","body":"Back heels (tripping), wrestling throws, and clinching are allowed.\nAny movement in the list, leaning on the barrier of the list, any holds and grips of the barrier of the list.\nA competitor can disarm any opponent by any authorized action, A competitor can take away a weapon from the belt of the opponent, provided the fighter holds their weapon. The fighter is then allowed to use the opponent’s weapon until the end of the round, and then it must be surrendered back to the opponent.\nOpposing fighters (who are armed) can take or knock down reserve weapons that are placed on a wide top bar list as long as supports are not holding them.\nGrappling the base of the skull but not the bottom edge of the helmet is permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"49b989e91a549d52c8447af774aabc77db6e60e4f90d48f9c35c50b803d83f51","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Weapon Loss","body":"A fighter must hold a weapon with at least one hand.\nIf a fighter is not holding their weapon with a hand, they are considered disarmed and are not authorized to perform any attacking actions until the grip on the weapon is restored.\n\nA fighter who has lost their weapon is allowed to:\n● Protect themself from the strikes without performing any offensive actions or holds.\n● Take a reserve weapon they had with them.\n● Take a reserve weapon from an ungrounded teammate in the list.\n● Take a reserve weapon from their teammate located in the allocated weapon distribution zone.\n● Grab a polearm which leans against the top rail of the barrier or its ungrounded teammate’s/owner’s body. In this case, it is not considered lying on the surface of the list.\n● Yield by kneeling.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.5","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a6858b0798a262ceb1597fda1275c44056cf00ffbafe26f22f3de499633d7678","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6","title":"Reserve Weapons","body":"","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.6","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"838e874af281f17b529438cb3da6c0c297a268454efe05c43b33ced9fff6487b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6.1","title":"Wide top bar list","body":"Reserve weapons must be placed on the top of the bar in the designated area for a fighter to pick up themselves. It is prohibited to pass a weapon to the fighter or hold the weapon when a fighter is taking it.\nThis will impose a penalty (See section 5 in “Buhurt Regulations” document).","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5"],"content_sha256":"0bf4d4df7cdb4caaefc16d9b4eece4b4a135689d65eec7a601bb6059fe17ee6c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6.2","title":"No wide top bar list","body":"Reserve weapons may be passed to the fighter from above the top rail of the list within the designated area.\nIt is prohibited to pass a weapon below the top rail of the list. This will impose a penalty (See section 5 in “Buhurt Regulations” document)","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:3.6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:3.6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["5"],"content_sha256":"deb3b27841d38f95681996750b31f849848c6df53b3cd670ec7573401a5b9203","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Prohibited Fighting Techniques","body":"Performance of any prohibited technique is a serious rules violation and is penalized with a verbal warning, yellow or red card. The penalty is imposed regardless of the fighter’s intent.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d1209311fd885e6f372fd0b72455df4241b00d91033dd4e8251b0fb158d0c54e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Unlisted Techniques","body":"Any actions not listed in section 4 above are prohibited. Only authorized techniques are permitted.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["4"],"content_sha256":"98a99541cc8a1c82ab6337ab311ec1d0d7f3bd856106641ce312ed1850c10d20","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Thrusting Actions","body":"Any thrusting actions with a weapon are prohibited. Threats of a thrusting action are also prohibited.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"44ae388641b717639c49400ef7861018cebd6eef392899f1634c3d73bf2c3fb4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Offensive Actions at Prohibited Strike Zones","body":"Any offensive actions that land on prohibited strike zones (See section 7 below) are prohibited.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["7"],"content_sha256":"8ad888b864cf3ccd6188e00085fe4c4a965e6eed72680f0c66691aff807d2c89","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Actions with Foot, Shin and Knee","body":"Actions with foot, shin, and knee aimed at the knee are prohibited. This includes actions that may cause the knee to hyperextend, such as push kicks to the thigh.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"046c1d59ff6779b35f595b149861a3231171f692f9fd6fb4a4402be0c9a958ee","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.5","title":"Grappling and Holds","body":"Grappling and holding with the hand on specific armor elements (aventail, edge of pauldrons, edge of the helmet), pushes on the bottom edge of the helmet and subsequent neck twists are prohibited.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.5","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"494fbb170b45fa3b89d7acde8892494dff7bf92b8e949fa07bcfc44d420c4264","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6","title":"Armor Tampering","body":"Deliberate attempts to remove any elements of the armor are prohibited.\nThe fighter committing the offense will be sat down and given a yellow card.\nA fighter who deliberately has their armor so it can be easily removed will receive a yellow card for unsportsmanlike conduct.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.6","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"02e8a32629da88c5e66ba54f45742b5ff264dea9a12f5f4f1560ba36f9f5b8d4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.7","title":"Suffocation Techniques","body":"Grips, clamps, suffocation techniques with direct pressure on the front, side and back of the neck (under or on top of the aventail) using any part of the body, equipment, or weapon are prohibited. A poorly fitted helmet does not count as a suffocating technique.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.7","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"32e8c7aa010c3373a3449aeb4da2842c62b894f8d3368704f6b63e96c6223ce4","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8","title":"Specific Strikes","body":"Strikes or punching with the head of a one-handed axe are prohibited if the grip of the hand is less than 30 cm away from the blade.\nStrikes with hammerheads are prohibited.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.8","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e207a4b4a7e16a25f67763522a7b9bbaeae7e7e0bd894caf7ba9d307ef17d67d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.9","title":"Dangerous Takedowns","body":"Any takedown that spikes an opponent on their head/neck and suplex (arch throws) variations are prohibited.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.9","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a23119669f8cc4e22aec2b69736ef5c73fe0d589ade812844bde114a9119f9a9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.10","title":"Intentional Passivity","body":"Intentional passivity and stalling of the action (such as an inactive clinch) are prohibited.\nAn inactive clinch is a clinch situation with the fighters performing weak weapon strikes or no grappling techniques aimed at grounding their opponent for 10 seconds or longer.\nThe strikes with a fist, knees, or shield, are not considered.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.10","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e0afad7c014871a3954e2cf82de1ea9645146803ca3fc512e94ad9629947eb3f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.11","title":"Joint Locks and Hyperextension","body":"Arm lock and leg lock techniques, and any actions that may cause a limb to hyperextend, are prohibited.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.11","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"83d39dfbc5f41caf4ead0c51a53571e6ac5a015db453ac12d0fdd93d083e351b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.12","title":"Striking Grounded competitors","body":"Striking a grounded competitor is prohibited.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.12","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4fb7e20f3ca1e78bf2d338fda8bd35949d618319e48d0c36a783c50506ba0041","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.13","title":"Injuring a competitor","body":"Deliberately injuring the fighter who has lost a defensive element of equipment.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.13","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cb714fac76e167d69dbd1bc5ecaa21defdb77e3aa52dc36183b9fe0c2d91d57d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.14","title":"Uncontrolled Strikes","body":"Any uncontrolled strikes and actions with a weapon.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.14","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d0974e78f1bb39386bb56dbb033f4a95e591d08a2afb38cdf5caa8a5e372e638","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.15","title":"Weapon Loss","body":"It is prohibited to pick up a weapon that is lying flat on the ground, to receive a weapon from an already grounded fighter, to receive a weapon from any area outside the list except for the designated area.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:4.15","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9ec7b3d478994d5fd4d11316cde6794938f06cdcd4f99bb2b5a4cab04f082205","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Other Prohibited Actions","body":"These rules contribute to maintaining the integrity, safety, and orderliness of the event. They cover aspects such as participant behavior, substance use, adherence to commands, and respect for officials and other attendees. The role of the Knight Marshal is highlighted in several instances, emphasizing their authority and responsibility in ensuring the proper conduct of the event.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"924883217d278a71c9784e0c072056aca7b66d9c34f728ebcdf29c861d699f93","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Leaving Lists","body":"Intentional leaving of the lists after the command “Start Fight” and before the announcement of the results of the fight is prohibited. Permission to leave must be granted by the Knight Marshal.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"90a46544bfbaf3388c0cfba2ecf1faa348fd0faf2a24b8a5e2ee1ae92e5726c2","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Interference from grounded competitors","body":"Grounded fighters:\n● must remain on the ground until the “All Rise” command of the Knight Marshal. They are not allowed to return to a standing position,\n● are not allowed to physically interfere in the course of the fight,\n● must maintain a comfortable seated or lying position until the end of the round. A comfortable position is a signal that the fighter is not injured,\n● are not allowed to change their position in the list unless there is a threat to their safety.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0630a5ebb2968fb55d78ac8e19507f444d2c8aca540b4e45ee11f11339579c4e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Equipment and Weapon Approval","body":"Competitors are not allowed to use any part of the equipment or any weapon that hasn't been allowed by the Authenticity Committee.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"943e910818c51e1a482535c896a33eec1fc0bd98803ce383caaf1a25a31ab6a3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4","title":"Substance Use","body":"It's not allowed for the competitor to be under the influence of alcohol or any psychoactive substances.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"01d0ef7bc6161f794f77da1df2752774ace64fc7764875a6200bdaa65d41658a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Offensive Actions Against Others","body":"Any offensive actions against marshals, corner support, spectators, or anyone else other than the current opponent are prohibited.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.5","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"442852ddfd03d2d358ccc0367e4ef19df487840f82a3f165441b961f40a02d3f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.6","title":"Event Interference","body":"Any actions made by a competitor or their support that may impede the course of the event are prohibited.\nFor a demonstration of poor sportsmanship, derogatory behavior, obscene language, commentaries directed at marshals, opponents, or spectators.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:5.6","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d81f734bb24c54bfc07567df976b09db4ba05d052c8ffa1dfc6bb1a287dcca33","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Prohibited Strike Zones","body":"These rules are designed to prioritize the safety of the participants by prohibiting strikes to vulnerable and potentially dangerous areas. The specific definitions and considerations for the base of the skull and back of the knee provide clarity on the prohibited strike zones. Striking the foot is allowed under certain circumstances, emphasizing the importance of situational awareness and control during combat. The overall intention is to prevent serious injuries and ensure a fair and safe competition.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"7cd79d399ee1c0ade6a0be0f9291cd3afdad352d4a94cff118695c3eb9b60ed3","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.1","title":"Back and Front of the Neck","body":"Strikes to the back and front of the neck are prohibited.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.1","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"010fc07da1ba574b743ed808a88b18a970cf2ef19fcdceb5b38fd114454baeb5","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.2","title":"Base of the Skull","body":"The base of the skull is considered a prohibited strike zone, specifically defined as the bottom third of the back of the helmet.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.2","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"85ac55a4434ebd1f27199f6778543afeaaaf0111a3f79766d2b970df0cb09f5b","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.3","title":"Back of the Knee","body":"Strikes to the back of the knee are prohibited. No pressure is to be placed on the back of the knee.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.3","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bcf6c34e30d629beb65bb12de7f9e4ccc28f3da98f0a3c77ce3f9309c2ee2cea","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.4","title":"Groin and Crotch","body":"Strikes to the groin and crotch are prohibited.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.4","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2c185bd842fc73f19100816324e276e6c845609f0ad06640a9c4d3a8501dfe55","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.5","title":"Feet and Ankle","body":"Strikes to the feet and ankles are prohibited. However, striking the foot is not considered a prohibited strike if the competitor raises their foot while the strike is already occurring.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.5","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"ad16b1b51ed4212013786c0ff9c02ec12aa1f327d934332fec81ad4cd9e38b8c","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":57,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"6.6","title":"Unprotected Body Parts","body":"Any part of the opponent’s body that has lost its protection is considered a prohibited strike zone.","page_from":12,"page_to":12,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:6.6","parent_key":"buhurt-rules:6","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b824eb584414030f78370270fd8d38a6930576f5862f8bc9374961e7c1349aae","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":58,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"7","title":"Management of the Fights","body":"Fights of the category are managed under the Buhurt International ‘Buhurt Regulations’ by penalties that are imposed depending on the situation in the list and fighters’ and marshals’ actions.","page_from":13,"page_to":13,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"cc9701b41f260ba3d92baab3c44ab46652263048b106064421eaac6cad73e1b6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":59,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"8","title":"Changelog","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way BI keeps transparent communication and clarity about the rules.\n\nApril - 2026 (V. 26.4.1) Suppression:\n- 3.5. Weapon Loss: “Grab a weapon left on the table top by an active fighter.”\n\nApril - 2026 (V. 26.4) Formatting redone for consistency and readability. Except points listed below, no content changes.\nGrammatical corrections were also made.\nClarification:\n- Section 2. Marshal Structure removed and added to Buhurt Regulations - Titles for 1.3.1. “Cases For Grounding” and 1.3.2. “Cases for Not Grounding”. No content changes except:\n- “While not carrying a weapon in your hand you're not allowed to engage in offensive actions [...]” to “While not carrying a weapon in their hand, they engaged in offensive actions [...]”\n- “Any part of a polearm, a sword blade or mace is not considered as contacting the ground.” yo “They touched the ground with any part of a weapon”.\nAdd:\n- 3.”Authorized Equipement”: Multiple references to AC documents for details.\n- 4.3. Weapon-Grabbing: “Grabbing your own blade by the hand is not allowed.”\n- 4.5. Weapon Loss: “Grab a weapon left on the table top by an active fighter.” Clarification:\n- 6.4.2. No “wide” top bar list\n- 4. Authorized Fighting Techniques: Introduction paragraph moved to 4.5. Weapon Loss section.\n\nUpdate: January-2026 -replaced: Various capitalization replacements throughout.\n-add: 1.3.1 Added heading.\n-add: 1.3.2 Added heading.\n-add: 2.1 Shall stop rounds with the “Hold” command and yellow flag between helmets of the fighters. The fighters must stop across the entire list and should not move.\n-clarification: 3.1.4 Medieval Shoes with low profile(non lugged/studded/spiked) soles as referenced in Authenticity Standards -add: 4.1 That is at the ready and unsheathed.\n-clarification: 5.3 Any offensive actions that land on prohibited strike zones (See section: 7. Prohibited Strike Zones) are prohibited.\n.\nUpdate: December-2024 -replaced: “Oral” with “Verbal” -add: 4.6.2 : This will impose a penalty (See article 5 in “Buhurt Regulations”) -add: 4.6.1 : This will impose a penalty (See article 5 in “Buhurt Regulations”) -add: 3.1 Reference ”Weapons requirements” for all the rules -add: 3.1 Reference “Weapons/Shield Chart” for sizes and weights\n\nUpdate date: March-2024\n- format: new design format, document will be used from now on.","page_from":14,"page_to":14,"stable_key":"buhurt-rules:8","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["2","5"],"content_sha256":"add67668cf9a3ac72dc703c40b2a3fc31697f713178bf0556e8e6b12d6b6523c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
select private.rules_import_version($rules${"governing_body":"Buhurt International","release":"2026-10-06","inventory_key":"marshal/duels-rules","synthetic":false,"version":{"version":"26.4","title":"Duels rules 26.4","published_on":null,"effective_from":null,"note":"Every page footer \"V. 26.4\" (the footer prints the title \"Buhurt Rules\", the document is the Duels rules); changelog entry \"April - 2026 (V. 26.4)\".","source_url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BsQVd3-9v_mp8l5DPj2p_jDUGn2hZPrD/view?usp=drive_link","source_sha256":"f20867141e8adf6c897cff6f1630d0cdf56fbfc6ad387d6c475a166854d6bd26","retrieved_at":"2026-10-06T00:00:00Z","page_count":11,"extractor":"pdftotext unknown -layout -enc UTF-8","content_sha256":"04ff3cd66a145b23f65b91f88635aa7f40f25cd3105a12f9eaed69081d13d673","detected":{"version":"26.4","date":null},"confirmed_by":"Claude Code (Pack 22 import), read from the official PDF: cover, page footers and changelog","reconciliation":{"ok":true,"errors":[],"warnings":["page(s) without extractable text: 1"],"pages":11,"source_lines":287,"assigned_lines":343,"furniture_lines":50,"unaccounted_lines":[],"double_assigned_lines":[],"char_coverage":0.99461,"provisions":56,"numbered":55,"needs_review":0,"verified":0,"empty_pages":[1],"rejected_numbers":0,"duplicate_numbers":[],"duplicate_texts":[],"version_confirmed":true,"source_sha256_matches":true,"ocr_lines":0,"picture_text_lines":0,"ocr_corrections":0}},"provisions":[{"ordinal":1,"depth":0,"kind":"figure","number":null,"title":null,"body":"","page_from":1,"page_to":1,"stable_key":"duels-rules:page-1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":"cover page: artwork only, no text","topics":["cover"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":2,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"1","title":"Striking Zones (legal vs illegal)","body":"","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0de315c84be319e9be7a3c448b8e86019b9172157793545da105d5331d83b51c","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":3,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.1","title":"Counted strike (legal strikes)","body":"During the fights of each category, the number of strikes by the blade of the weapon delivered into the legal strike zone of the opponent’s body is counted.\nA counted strike is considered a strike if it was clear and deliberate, and the opponent failed to counter it effectively with a defensive action.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fd70fdc476b7da87002f41637634a7d7b0d734692376c489100523a0e1a7cbbf","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":4,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2","title":"Prohibited Strike Zones (illegal strikes)","body":"The following zones are “illegal strikes” and will not count for your score. Striking into these zones can result in penalties or disqualification.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"69c7b200ae00921380b512a7d6907d699d27e2ccdd6e8e8a83e2af778a178e7a","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":5,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.1","title":"Back and Front of the Neck","body":"Strikes to the back and front of the neck are prohibited.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1e2d8e64fb481397ef3783ff015df71c4bebd98b44511a7d6194c204af710cbd","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":6,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.2","title":"Base of Skull","body":"The base of the skull is considered a prohibited strike zone, specifically defined as the bottom third of the back of the helmet.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c9c89885a34eb2087c2b0c70bebd88539ae814bdffc1de16714be07fb5775be0","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":7,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.3","title":"Back of Knee","body":"Strikes to the back of the knee are prohibited. No pressure is to be placed on the back of the knee.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"70ab91e9cd267e4ab33049909bed5337f41d03be1baf3832931654d00d9139a7","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":8,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.4","title":"Groin and Crotch","body":"Strikes to the groin and crotch are prohibited.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"eb43b4a77d7cdd0c4affdf6e883f29ec4b0c0c368da610bd1e7a1ddbd37e558e","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":9,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.5","title":"Feet and Ankles","body":"Strikes to the feet and ankles are prohibited. However, striking the foot is not considered a prohibited strike if the competitor raises their foot while the strike is already occurring.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.5","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b5c83ef7f158bb16cfdbb3d90d17366e4155a6d72c639a332647d4a17fb2d5ae","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":10,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"1.2.6","title":"Unprotected Body Parts","body":"Any part of the opponent’s body that has lost itself protection is considered a prohibited strike zone.","page_from":3,"page_to":3,"stable_key":"duels-rules:1.2.6","parent_key":"duels-rules:1.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9b412f561260a6f58bf5b666572fdd2d088e130c0bc53ee7a591694dd55889b2","has_figures":true,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":11,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"2","title":"Scoring and Rounds","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a1115481ffcc77a4498c4b64a15528320f6698b607c0dcce3215a9614ebaadaf","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":12,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1","title":"Scoring","body":"","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c7eee7c8ef5763cfc8c6e822fe05d14ecae843ee52101caa5dacf18796ca7b02","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":13,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.1","title":"Sword and Shield","body":"Each strike to the legal striking zone of the opponent will score:\n● 2 points:\n○ Head ○ Torso\n● 1 point:\n○ Legs ○ Arms ○ Hands","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.1.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"bb037facf1037635a830b2b59eab5ce1b524d6d98d9a3c99b3cdcf032b953373","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":14,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.2","title":"Sword and Buckler","body":"Each strike to the legal striking zone of the opponent will score:\n● 1 point","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.1.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"73eec0c7c370fc9ccc7f6c63f054b86a2c254c9f531a121a891fe9f509c1ce94","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":15,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.3","title":"Polearm","body":"The full length of the cutting edge of the weapon is considered a blade.\nOffensive actions with the haft of the polearm do not score.\nThe grip must be held with 2 hands for a strike to be counted.\n\nEach strike to the legal striking zone of the opponent will score:\n● 0 point:\n○ Hands\n● 1 point:\n○ All other legal striking zones","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.1.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"152cff069813b2c91c048d9d5ac58ee67cbf1c01ea0ba7048a58492eca7fcc43","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":16,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.1.4","title":"Longsword","body":"Each strike to the legal striking zone of the opponent will score:\n2 hands holding the grip:\n● 2 points:\n○ Head ○ Torso\n● 1 point:\n○ Arms ○ Legs ○ Hands 1 hand holding the grip:\n● 1 point:\n○ All legal striking zones","page_from":4,"page_to":4,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.1.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.1","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"21ecc5321b557a750309de3cc8d1a5ca7dc69c54d1803f84f4b292313fb31a92","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":17,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2","title":"Rounds, Matches and Winning Conditions","body":"","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d11c730e1571308747aa2d02b8b370a016dc77a1e8327db59b1930bf2c196156","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":18,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.1","title":"Sword and Buckler","body":"A match is won by the first competitor who has 2 round victories.\nA round is won by the competitor who has either:\n● scored 5 points first before the time limit, or\n● scored more points than their opponent if the time limit has been reached.\nThe maximum score for a round is 5 points.\nThe maximum time limit for a round is 1 minute.\nThere is no break in between rounds.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.2.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"a56b68697343aa9d83e9e6c1ac40ae255b0553e5a43d4a0d9a3c123372b2e6e3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":19,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.2.2","title":"Polearm, Longsword and Sword and Shield","body":"A match is won by the competitor who has scored at least 2 more points than their opponent during the overall match.\nThe score of the match is the sum of the scores of the rounds.\nA match consists of 2 main rounds of 1 minute each.\nIf the score difference between the 2 competitors is less than 2 points after the 2 main rounds, additional 30-second rounds are fought until the 2-point difference is reached.\nThere is a 30-second break in between rounds.\n\nImportant!\nThe organizers can change the length of the round, provided this decision is coordinated with the Head Organization and is registered in the Tournament Regulations.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.2.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0bd625881269ee67002c6047a6dde16d906e131dd1349e5d7ca9c1b8c8e1545b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":20,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3","title":"Technical win","body":"A “technical win” is awarded to one of the competitors in the following cases:","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:2","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"29a8cc2885723cb6f1455f66ba55f55bcd029c30329fae08aeb9cced286a7c58","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":21,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3.1","title":"Withdrawal","body":"A competitor is considered as withdrawn is they either:\n● Failed to report to the list upon the Head Referee’s call.\n● Failed to prepare the equipment within the designated time.\n● Withdraws before the match has started.\nThe competitor who failed to report to the list for the match may be penalized by a yellow card.\nIn the case a competitor cannot participate in the competition because of an injury or disqualification, their opponent is awarded a technical win.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.3.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"fda6b08faafdbd4e58accbe02ae0da1ca394899a00ed2ef236d2fd106690d275","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":22,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3.2","title":"Injury","body":"If the competitor cannot continue the match due to the injury caused by an illegal strike, their opponent receives a penalty of a red card and is banned from further participation in the tournament.\nThe severity of the injury must be assessed by the designated medics of the tournament.\nThe injured competitor is awarded a technical win.\nThe injured competitor is withdrawn from further matches in this category.","page_from":5,"page_to":5,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.3.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"986af6b3873d18b2e2100b670afa5d20e5d6f73e74dc75327cb7a38bf8e72246","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":23,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3.3","title":"Disqualification of the opponent","body":"If a competitor gets 2 yellow cards or 1 red card, all their following opponents are awarded a technical win.","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.3.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1bff20d30246a4bb51da2288876641f5601a63230f0c0f9620f9e3ea82611650","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":24,"depth":2,"kind":"rule","number":"2.3.4","title":"Armor failure","body":"If the match is impeded due to equipment failure that is impossible to fix within the designated time frame of 1 minute.\n\nScoring for “technical win” 5-0 for 2 rounds for Sword and Buckler category 10-0 per round for all other categories","page_from":6,"page_to":6,"stable_key":"duels-rules:2.3.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:2.3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"4e73d18050b31f4f4577609bb7218a2a045f220247c13f2313226a0418d8e5c9","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":25,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"3","title":"Authorized Fighting Techniques","body":"These rules aim to define a set of permitted and prohibited actions to ensure the safety of participants while engaging in combat.\n\nThe guidelines cover striking, grabbing, and various techniques to maintain a fair and controlled environment during the event.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"63e57be7ee813b6f2dcf85bba5c2126415344a23e3845e080a9e18089cf2a930","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":26,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.1","title":"Permitted Strikes","body":"Strikes with the blade and the haft of the weapon are permitted.\nBuckler: Strikes with the flat of the buckler are permitted.\nPolearm: Strikes with a free hand, if they have a weapon in the other hand, are permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f75923d3f335b3ba28a8c3947f3065af09e639a7aaef2e36bbd89ad34510687f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":27,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.2","title":"Strike Zones","body":"Strikes to any area not mentioned as a prohibited strike zone are permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c348ed7d346f214e2658ee48a0dfc03503061bc696d01fe690ff940b3f695bb5","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":28,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.3","title":"Parry","body":"Parrying the opponent’s strikes is permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"028e8321d6643e39681a73a70fb57f7eecd77c5a4779b9ebeb8a4d7e7004521b","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":29,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.4","title":"Techniques and moves with shields (Buckler, Sword and Shield)","body":"Pushing the opponent with the shoulder or the flat of the shield is permitted.\nPushing the blade, shield, armed hand or upper body (above the waistline) of the opponent with the flat or edge of the shield is permitted.\nUsing the shield to hook or cover the opponent’s shield is permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"e05c5c44c549e75e4854062d9fa629534e9d6f6dc3045b93c8e133e4e14e31db","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":30,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.5","title":"Techniques and moves (Longsword, Polearm)","body":"Pushing the opponent with the blade or arms is permitted.\nPushing off the opponent's arms with the arms is permitted.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.5","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f1b50b78031f0a0d257fb3a176b2b9ea6e37f59a2dd891941bab5d7c9762fc7e","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":31,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.6","title":"Weapon-Grabbing","body":"Participants are allowed to grab their own weapon (except the blade) with their hands.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.6","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"83c3a85f531c1576a8ef7e40d2ef4d15ccffda57646515aa33f617c8dffbe3dd","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":32,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"3.7","title":"Pinned to the List Rail","body":"Pinning an opponent to the list is not against the rules; however, if a competitor is pinned against the list rail, the Knight Marshal will call 'Break Fight' and reset the competitors to the center of the list.","page_from":7,"page_to":7,"stable_key":"duels-rules:3.7","parent_key":"duels-rules:3","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8df34a1c5b6ff1bce5aae8679c75dc1b0c5df3298ed87acb85967a2cb3149ac0","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":33,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"4","title":"Prohibited Fighting Techniques","body":"These rules aim to ensure the safety, fairness, and adherence to a set of standards.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"c48d119d1caa0537f2bc0b79c01e7f2e8752c7369cc19b4d71855ca3ac693521","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":34,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.1","title":"Unlisted Techniques","body":"Any actions not listed in section 3 (Authorized Fighting Techniques) of the rules are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":["3"],"content_sha256":"4e286ebd3ce8a1313ec6818f4d0a207f8272f123478b53b5d5fd6096ff6fec70","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":35,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.2","title":"Thrusting Actions","body":"Any thrusting action with a weapon is prohibited.\nThreats of a thrusting action are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1eb9a3fe8af1ff0dc633c1c53e29a010a639becdc82f556af1b120b5d2796b17","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":36,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.3","title":"Offensive Actions on Prohibited Strike Zones","body":"Any offensive action landing on any prohibited strike zone is prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"1eccf2278341e70fba9bd27a09561bc1c6c5f2b322250df01a50c8ef6dd7ddfe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":37,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.4","title":"Striking to Grounded or Rising Competitors","body":"Striking a grounded or rising competitor is prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"6e6c82aa18417e203bf120e6759cfdc131ef57f779b51c68b8e554a6189e535a","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":38,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.5","title":"Strikes to Disarmed Opponent","body":"Strikes to an opponent who has lost their weapon are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.5","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"718c8e9549de3917e83298e2c81f42af4bef270d3b3fc00f18b83562442ac5fe","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":39,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.6","title":"Strikes with the Head","body":"Strikes to an opponent with the head are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.6","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"b6185d6c9d8f89cb2bae08f97cf9467be1daf33dd9f11d294dc00579e674d022","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":40,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.7","title":"Strikes with Legs","body":"Strikes with feet, shin, and knees are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.7","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"76dca2f9d02960eb9f200611703d813777fa30ebb54721c12b7845249afc4741","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":41,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.8","title":"Techniques and Moves","body":"Back heels, wrestling throws, and clinching are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.8","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"75c14d0a32b83b5aa9afb059151711645acbcf26ff4bbfa173e97fb8e87e5866","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":42,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.9","title":"Strikes with Hands and Elbows","body":"Strikes with hands and elbows are prohibited, with the exception of the Polearm category.\nSee “3.1. Permitted Strikes” for details.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.9","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"8b0ce72dfa9805389cc0f0f55e7b6489682373ae34bfa60fde1e6312504daf55","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":43,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.10","title":"Strikes with the pommel or cross guard of a Bladed Weapon","body":"Strikes delivered with the pommel or cross guard of a bladed weapon are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.10","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"d20d5e45de2d9d176ebd24b6ad3e854b8d2f7f0570068e81e97fd72d112049f7","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":44,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.11","title":"Grappling","body":"Grappling with hands and arms to the opponent’s torso, head, and limbs.\nHandholds of the opponent’s sword.\nTrap opponents' weapons by shield, buckler and/or arm/hands.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.11","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"0c906be0e2112eb452b45a40be2420ea966e959dc9059fbb83de087f5bfa9f27","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":45,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.12","title":"Strikes with a Shield","body":"Strikes delivered with the edge of a shield are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.12","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"9b5f131638ef1b9d9b27927bb45fe952bf42d8c0c9c5f5919653704506a6318f","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":46,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"4.13","title":"Strikes with a Buckler","body":"Strikes with the edge of a buckler are prohibited.","page_from":8,"page_to":8,"stable_key":"duels-rules:4.13","parent_key":"duels-rules:4","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"5b0e74919c887487e9c1eadcb9dea29faa0fd89b639ff06af4421a6664f75604","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":47,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"5","title":"Authorized Equipment","body":"These rules aim to ensure a high standard of authenticity, safety, and historical accuracy in the equipment and conduct of the participants.\n\nReference all Authenticity Committee documents for the detailed rules.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"57723e87420e1a35dd0d6b517b6a2964e20442afd6ccadb5ded388b5845b1ff3","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":48,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.1","title":"Technical and Authentic Compliance","body":"All equipment must meet Buhurt International technical and authentic requirements.\nReference:\n● “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” document for the rules.\n● ”Technical Requirements for Weapons” document.\n● ”Technical Requirements for Armors” document.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.1","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"2313804c614c4fc5097c1ad5597f7c79478a4dcc7af299a3fea665ec29dc7160","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":49,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.2","title":"Competitor Eligibility","body":"Competitors are not allowed unless they have passed technical and authenticity checks.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.2","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"db07382d5b570febc4d5427170d015b7581bac6213dc5211f99be93fe62e1c07","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":50,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.3","title":"Weapon Requirements","body":"Reference ”Technical Requirements for Weapons” document for all the rules.\nReference “Weapons/Shield Chart” document for sizes and weights.\nReminder: Low-quality, dirty, rusty, or historically implausible weapons are not allowed.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.3","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"23a38ad47d2264ec5135471ece98798f5e8a7c42177d41a67f88031819507093","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":51,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.4","title":"Footwear","body":"Reference ”Textiles and Leather” document for details.\nReminder: Only medieval Shoes with low profile (non-lugged/studded/spiked) are allowed.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.4","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"79f131f798553a270535d12df163bcde8bad0df1e520b878634c1832c3f11983","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":52,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.5","title":"Materials","body":"Reference ”Textiles and Leather” document for details.\nReminder: Modern adhesive tape, plastic ties, and other visible modern materials are not permitted.\nTextile adhesive tape of neutral colors for kit repair is an exception.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.5","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"243271cf6322d6c455697a70d22939e9478726fc959e9f0295eff952ae232981","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":53,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.6","title":"Decorations","body":"Reference “Armors and Weapons Aesthetics and Decorations” for details.\nReminder: Slogans and imagery on equipment should be historically plausible and not derogatory.\nNo modern equipment or decorations are allowed.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.6","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"aefa1d435ec0435e03783a443cb61a1a1ba248fe95c979adc98f102b0b7d748c","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":54,"depth":1,"kind":"rule","number":"5.7","title":"Equipment Changes","body":"Participants are allowed to change elements of equipment (armor or weapon) during intervals or due to breakage.\nTechnical Marshal supervision is required for equipment changes.","page_from":9,"page_to":9,"stable_key":"duels-rules:5.7","parent_key":"duels-rules:5","review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"f9af2f4712710163d910a11dd8c1a20f8a530c706f8596437d98c62a49112cee","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":55,"depth":0,"kind":"section","number":"6","title":"Management of the competitors","body":"Management of the competitors is conducted in accordance with the Buhurt International Duels Regulations, with penalties that are imposed depending on the situation in the list and competitors’ and marshals’ actions.","page_from":10,"page_to":10,"stable_key":"duels-rules:6","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":[],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"aa9518e7edc98104c8136adc53d98f750141631fc108b5112d3ec457aaa98a4d","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"},{"ordinal":56,"depth":0,"kind":"note","number":"7","title":"Changelog","body":"This will be the change log of this document. It will be updated regularly and will display what has been removed/added/reworded/formatted. This way BI keeps transparent communication and clarity about the rules.\n\nApril - 2026 (V. 26.4) Formatting redone for consistency and readability. Except points listed below, no content changes.\nGrammatical corrections were also made.\nClarification:\n- Titles for 1.3.1. “Cases For Grounding” and 1.3.2. “Cases for Not Grounding”. No content changes except:\n- “While not carrying a weapon in your hand you're not allowed to engage in offensive actions [...]” to “While not carrying a weapon in their hand, they engaged in offensive actions [...]”\n- “Any part of a polearm, a sword blade or mace is not considered as contacting the ground.” yo “They touched the ground with any part of a weapon”.\nAdd:\n- 3.”Authorized Equipement”: Multiple references to AC documents for details.\n- 4.3. Weapon-Grabbing: “Grabbing your own blade by the hand is not allowed.”\n- 4.5. Weapon Loss: “Grab a weapon left on the table top by an active fighter.” Clarification:\n- 6.4.2. No “wide” top bar list\n- 4. Authorized Fighting Techniques: Introduction paragraph moved to 4.5. Weapon Loss section.\nAdd:\n- 2.3.2. Injury: “The severity of the injury must be assessed by the designated medics of the tournament.” Clarification:\n- 2.3. Technical win: scores are per round\n- 4.3. Offensive Actions on Prohibited Strike Zones: “Any offensive action landing on any prohibited strike zone is prohibited.”\n- Split of 4.9. Punches and elbow strikes in: 4.9.Strikes with Hands and Elbows and 4.13.\nSuppression:\n- 5.1. General Requirements: title has been removed for uselessness. Subsequent titles have been moved up.\nAdd:\n- 5. ”Authorized Equipement”: Multiple references to AC documents for details.\n\nUpdate: January 2026 -add: 2.2.1 In case of a draw, fight additional rounds until one competitors has two round victories -add: 4.11 Trap opponents' weapons by shield, buckler and/or arm/hands.\n-add: 5.1.4 Medieval Shoes with low profile (non lugged/studded/spiked) soles as referenced in Authenticity Standards.\n\nUpdate: october 2025\n- add: 1.2.\n\nUpdate: March 2025 -add: 3.7 Pinned to the List Rail\n\nTo see older changelogs, please refer to the archived documents.","page_from":11,"page_to":11,"stable_key":"duels-rules:7","parent_key":null,"review_status":"extracted","review_note":null,"topics":["changelog"],"keywords":[],"cross_refs":[],"content_sha256":"3136135a1be8b6a24aab98e85792cd8728dc662908d52aab8dbd0751f21064a6","has_figures":false,"extraction":"text"}]}$rules$::jsonb);
